Linux
---------

Linux is an operating system commonly used to run enterprise applications and servers.

For example, our Java application might run on a Linux server with Apache Tomcat/JBoss installed.

As an engineer, we use Linux commands to:

- Navigate directories.
- Check application logs.
- Search for errors.
- Check whether processes are running.
- Check disk and memory usage.
- Investigate application failures.

A. Basic Linux commands
-------------------------
pwd - Show current directory > pwd
ls  -	List files > ls -l
cd  - Change directory > cd /opt/jboss
mkdir - 	Create directory > mkdir logs
touch -	Create empty file	touch > test.txt
cp - Copy files > cp a.txt b.txt
mv - Move/rename files > mv old.txt new.txt
rm - Delete files > rm test.txt
cat - Display file content > cat app.log
less - Read large files	> less app.log
clear - Clear > terminal	clear
